Wrong (A): A volumetric attack overwhelms network bandwidth capacity through sheer traffic volume rather than exploiting protocol-level handshake mechanics.
Wrong (B): An application layer attack targets specific application functions such as HTTP requests or database queries, not the TCP connection establishment process.
Wrong (C): A social engineering attack manipulates human behavior through deception; it is not a category of DDoS attack and does not involve flooding network protocols.$EXPL$
