-- Q3647: Security Controls and Monitoring [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under NIST SP 800-53 Section 3 (Security and Privacy Controls), controls are categorized by when they operate in the incident lifecycle. Preventive controls stop events before occurrence, detective controls identify events during or after occurrence, and corrective controls remediate impact after detection. For example, badge readers prevent unauthorized entry, cameras detect suspicious activity, and account disablement corrects an active compromise.
Wrong (B): The three control types serve distinct purposes at different points in the incident lifecycle and are not interchangeable.
